Bugfix: Add accessible names to the checkboxes in the file conflict dialog

The checkboxes that select which version of a conflicting file to keep had no
accessible name. Screen readers announced up to four unnamed checkboxes in a
row, so there was no way to tell which one keeps the new and which one keeps
the existing file - a decision that overwrites data.

The real input is positioned off screen and the visible box is drawn by the
pseudo element of the following label, so the label is what users actually
operate. Binding it via for/id gives the checkbox a name composed of the file
name, the modification date and the size. The click handler that used to
compensate for a missing binding has been removed, because the browser now
forwards label clicks natively.

Two text colours of the same dialog were raised to meet the minimum contrast
ratio: the file name from #777777 (4.48:1) to #757575, and the read-only
message from #e9322d (4.23:1) to #d93025.

